  <section id="ws-panel-text" class="workshop-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="ws-tab-text" hidden><div class="workshop-import"><div><h2>The list as text</h2><p>Edit the whole list at once, or paste over it. Moxfield, Archidekt, Arena, MTGO, CSV and share links all work; unfinished lists are kept as drafts, and a pasted list’s Maybeboard and Sideboard sections go to those boards. To bring in a new deck, use <button type="button" class="link-button" data-deck-act="import">Import</button>.</p><div class="ws-text-head"><label for="ws-text">Decklist · saved as you type</label><button type="button" id="ws-file-pick" class="glass tiny">Open file…</button><input type="file" id="ws-file" accept=".txt,.dek,.dck,.cod,.csv,.tsv,.md,text/plain,text/csv,text/markdown,application/xml,text/xml" hidden/></div><textarea id="ws-text" spellcheck="false" placeholder="COMMANDER
1 Your commander

1 Sol Ring
…"></textarea><div id="ws-boards-text"></div><label for="ws-source">Source link <small>optional, saved with the deck</small></label><input id="ws-source" type="url" placeholder="Original deck URL"/></div><aside><h3 id="ws-export-heading">Export &amp; share</h3><div id="ws-export-panel"></div><details class="ws-formats"><summary>Supported formats</summary><p>Moxfield, Archidekt, MTG Arena, MTGO (.txt / .dek), MTGGoldfish, TappedOut, Deckstats, EDHREC, Scryfall, Forge and XMage .dck, Cockatrice .cod, collection-app CSV (ManaBox, Dragon Shield, Delver Lens, Deckbox, TCGplayer), markdown or bulleted lists, a Project Commander share link, or a file dropped on the list. Category headings like “Creatures (30)” or “## Ramp” are understood, and lines that aren’t cards are listed for you. A COMMANDER block or “Commander: Name” marks your commander; add a second for a legal partner. Quantities, set codes, collector numbers and foils survive exports; the Maybeboard and Sideboard stay with the deck but out of the list.</p></details></aside></div></section>
